  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\cos ^{-1} x-\\cos ^{-1} \\frac{y}{2}=\\alpha$, then $4 x^2-4 x y \\cos \\alpha+y^2$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "cbYYK",
      "text": "\n$2 \\sin 2 \\alpha$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bO6rB",
      "text": "\n4\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "BfKu8",
      "text": "\n$4 \\sin ^2 \\alpha$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "3FMbw",
      "text": "\n$-4 \\sin ^2 \\alpha$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\cos ^{-1} x-\\cos ^{-1} \\frac{y}{2}=\\alpha \\\\\n& \\cos ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{x y}{2}+\\sqrt{\\left(-x^2\\right)\\left(1-\\frac{y^2}{4}\\right)}\\right)=\\alpha \\\\\n& \\cos ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{x y+\\sqrt{4-y^2-4 x^2+x^2 y^2}}{2}\\right)=\\alpha \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow 4-y^2-4 x^2+x^2 y^2=4 \\cos ^2 \\alpha+x^2 y^2-4 x y \\cos \\alpha \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow 4 x^2+y^2-4 x y \\cos \\alpha=4 \\sin ^2 \\alpha\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
